-- title:
--   Degree ℓ+1 of the ℓ-degeneracy inclusion when p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $p$, let $M\ge 1$ satisfy $p\mid M$ and $p^2\nmid M$, and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\neq p$. Here $\Gamma_H(N)$ denotes the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ consisting of the matrices in $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose lower-right entry lies in the given subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/N)^\times$, and for a subgroup $\Gamma$ the field $F_K(\Gamma)=$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) is the $K$-subfield of the Laurent series field over $K$ generated by all quotients of the reductions to $K$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of the same weight on $\Gamma$ (the denominator reduction being nonzero). The conclusion is twofold: the degree of the inclusion [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaModLH`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L132) of $F_K(\Gamma_H(M))$ into $F_K(\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell))$, i.e. the rank of the target as a module over the source via this embedding, equals $\ell+1$; and the relative degree of the two intermediate fields $F_K(\Gamma_H(M))\subseteq F_K(\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell))$ of $K((q))$ is likewise $\ell+1$.
--
--   This computes the degree of the first degeneracy (Hecke) inclusion of $q$-expansion function fields in characteristic $p$ at a level divisible exactly once by $p$: the $\Gamma_0(p)$-part of the level is invisible on $q$-expansions mod $p$, so the degree is the one obtained at the good level $M/p$, namely the index $\ell+1$ of $\Gamma_0(\ell)$. It feeds the computation of the reduced root function of a Hecke operator in terms of the norm along the companion embedding `heckeBetaModLH`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrankAlong_heckeAlphaModLH_eq_and_relfinrank_eq_add_one_of_charP_of_dvd.lean

